course: dictionary
lesson: 6821
title: Ostracism: being left out
level: primary-6
stars: 1
explain: Ostracism means leaving someone out on purpose, so they are not included in a group. It can happen in a playground, a club or a class. You do not need to shout or hit anyone for it to hurt. Ignoring someone and making sure they are never picked can hurt just as much as unkind words.
explain: The word also has a history meaning. «Once a year Athenians could vote to send a too-powerful politician away for ten years by scratching his name on a bit of broken pottery called an ostrakon; this is called ostracism.» Look at the clues: a vote, a name on pottery, and being sent away. Together they show that ostracism in this sense is a formal way of removing someone from a city.
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. In a friendship story, ostracism is about people being left out. In a history lesson, it is about a vote. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then check by swapping your meaning in.
fact: Ostracism is a noun, and it is uncountable.
fact: Ostracism means deliberately leaving someone out so they are not included by a group.
fact: «Ostrakon» means a broken piece of pottery.
fact: In ancient Athens, ostracism was a vote to send a powerful citizen away from the city for ten years.
fact: Ostracism can hurt as much as words, even though nobody shouts or hits.
exercise: What does ostracism mean? | Giving someone a present for their birthday | *Leaving someone out on purpose | Winning a race at sports day | Writing a letter to a faraway friend
exercise: Mia sits alone while her group plays. Which is an example of ostracism? | *Her group keeps her out of every game on purpose | Her group shares their snacks with her | Her group sings a song together | Her group helps her finish her homework
exercise: In ancient Athens, what was written on an ostrakon? | A poem about the sea | A shopping list for the market | A recipe for vegetable soup | *The name of a powerful politician, to vote him away
test: «Once a year Athenians could vote to send a too-powerful politician away for ten years.» How long was the politician sent away? | A whole lifetime | Five days | *Ten years | One week
test: Why can ostracism hurt so much? | It makes people louder and more excited | *It leaves someone feeling alone and unwanted | It only happens in history books | It is always done by a teacher
exam: Which sentence best explains ostracism in friendships? | Writing a name on a piece of broken pottery | Sharing a joke with the whole class | Helping a friend carry their bag home | *Deliberately leaving a classmate out of the group
